Prerequisites
- Install Podman Destop
- podman ps
- podman compose up

1. Create Public Repository in Quay.io (website) -> podmano/users-ws-k8s

2. Open the application and run the below command to dockerize the application
	
	mvn -DskipTests package
	
	podman login quay.io
	
	podman build -t podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.0 .
	
	podman tag podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.0 quay.io/podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.0
	
3. Push the docker image into Podman

	podman push quay.io/podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.0
	
4. Create Kubernetes DEPLOYMENT

   kubectl create deployment user-ms-deployment --image quay.io/podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.0 --port=8082 --replicas=3

5. Check the Deployment status

	kubectl get deployments
	
6. Check the PODs status

	kubectl get pods
	
7. View the deployment details (Replicas, Events, Image, Port, StrategyType, Container Specification etc., )

	kubectl describe deployment user-ms-deployment
	
	or 
	
	kubectl describe deployment/user-ms-deployment
	
8. Expose the deployment for Service discovery (Types like ClusterIP, LoadBalancer, NodePort, Ingress, ExternalName)

	kubectl expose deployment user-ms-deployment --type=LoadBalancer --port=8082 --target-port=8082 --name users-ms-service
	
9. Get Kubernetes Service status

	kubectl get services
	
10. View Service details (Get the Pods endpoint i.e, IP addresses)

	kubectl describe service users-ms-service
	
11. View the Kubernetes setup in Docker Desktop & Test the application using Postman

12. Make some changes in the Application to redeploy

	mvn -DskipTests package
	
13. Rebuild the Docker with new TAG

	docker build -t podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.1 .
	
14. Push the revised Docker container into Docker Hub

	docker push podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.1
	
15. Update the Deployment with revised docker image (Deployment Name -> user-ms-deployment, Container Name -> users-ws-k8s)

	kubectl set image deployment/user-ms-deployment users-ws-k8s=podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.1
	
	Note: Old PODs get deleted and new PODs get Created
	
16. View the ROLLOUT history of the Deployment

	kubectl rollout history deployment/user-ms-deployment
	
17. Add details about Deployment changes via ANNOTATE 

	kubectl annotate deployment/user-ms-deployment kubernetes.io/change-cause="Updated docker image into podmano/users-ws-k8s:1.0.1"
	
18. View the PODs (Deleted old pods and Created 3 new pods)

	kubectl get pods
	
19. Set ENVIRONMENT variable and apply into the Deployment

	kubectl set env deployment/user-ms-deployment SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=test LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
	
	Note: Using this step, deployment add ANNOTATE automatically using the last time message.
	
20. Verify all the pods environment variables

	kubectl set env pods --all --list
	
21. Update the default-message ANNOTATE for the last rollout

	kubectl annotate deployment/user-ms-deployment kubernetes.io/change-cause="Set environment variables SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=test, LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG"
	
22. Remove a specific ENVIRONMENT variable

	kubectl set env deployment/user-ms-deployment LOG_LEVEL-
	
	kubectl annotate deployment/user-ms-deployment kubernetes.io/change-cause="Removed environment variable LOG_LEVEL"
	
23. ROLLOUT previous revision deployment

	kubectl rollout undo deployment/user-ms-deployment
	
	kubectl annotate deployment/user-ms-deployment kubernetes.io/change-cause="LOG_LEVEL environment variable back to deployment/pods"
	
24. ROLLOUT to a specific revision deployment

	kubectl rollout undo deployment/user-ms-deployment --to-revision=2
	
	kubectl rollout status deployment/user-ms-deployment
	
25. SCALE-UP  / SCALE-DOWN Replicas

	kubectl scale deployment/user-ms-deployment --replicas=1
	
	or 
	
	kubectl scale deployment/user-ms-deployment --replicas=5
	
26. View all PODs log

	kubectl logs -f deployment/user-ms-deployment --all-pods --max-log-requests=10

27. Get Kubernetes -> Control plane statistics in default way without Metrics server

	podman exec kind-control-plane crictl stats --all | Select-String "users-ws-k8s"

28. Kubernetes way of getting Metrics using server

	kubectl apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server/releases/latest/download/components.yaml
	
	Set-Content -Path patch.json -Value '[{"op":"add","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args/-","value":"--kubelet-insecure-tls"}]' -Encoding ascii
kubectl patch deployment metrics-server -n kube-system --type=json --patch-file patch.json

	wait about a minute, then

	kubectl top pods -l app=user-ms-deployment --sort-by=memory
	kubectl top pods -l app=user-ms-deployment --sort-by=cpu

	or 

	podman exec desktop-control-plane crictl stats --all | Select-String "users-ws-k8s"

	kubectl top nodes
	kubectl top pods

29. Get API versions in Kubernetes for all types of resources

	kubectl api-versions

30. Pod creation YML file with property when there is any changes in it -> imagePullPolicy {Always, IfNotPresent, Never}
    Always - if there is a change in the image then update the pod
	IfNotPresent - 
	Never - Don't revise the pods image eventhough a revised image is available

31. Check the POD size (CPU/RAM) existing limit

	kubectl get deployment user-ms-deployment -o jsonpath="{range .spec.template.spec.containers[*]}{.name}{'\n'}CPU request: {.resources.requests.cpu}{'\n'}CPU limit: {.resources.limits.cpu}{'\n'}{end}"

	or

	kubectl get pods -l app=user-ms-deployment -o custom-columns="POD:.metadata.name,CPU_REQ:.spec.containers[*].resources.requests.cpu,CPU_LIM:.spec.containers[*].resources.limits.cpu"

32. Set/Reset the POD CPU limit

	kubectl set resources deployment/user-ms-deployment -c=users-ws-k8s --requests=cpu=50m --limits=cpu=100m

33. View all the Deployment related ENVIRONMENT variables

	kubectl exec -it deploy/user-ms-deployment -- env

34. Forcefully route the traffic to a specific pod

	kubectl port-forward pod/user-ms-deployment-7f67689797-6cnjs 8082:8082

35. Cleanup / Destroy (pods, nodes, control plane, deployment, cluster)

	kubectl get all
	kubectl delete service users-ms-service
	kubectl delete deployment user-ms-deployment
	kubectl delete -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server/releases/latest/download/components.yaml

	

